s licenses software modules. The company's solutions are used in automotive video recorders, electronic mirrors, front advanced driver assistance system camera, AI Telematics Systems, and cabin monitoring system and driver monitoring system cameras in automotive field; central domain controllers for autonomous vehicles in autonomy; enterprise and public class, and home security cameras in the field of IoT; and enterprise, home, public spaces, and consumer applications, as well as for video conferencing, access control, healthcare, medical, and virtual reality applications. It sells its solutions to original design manufacturers, original equipment manufacturers, automotive market, and Tier-1 suppliers through its direct sales force and distributors. The company operates in Taiwan, rest of the Asia Pacific, Europe, the United States, and rest of North America. Ambarella, Inc. was incorporated in 2004 and is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Feng-Ming  Wang Ph.D. | Co-Founder, President, CEO & Executive Chairman | Age 61 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 959 people. Revenue per employee of $407K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $60K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $102K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Ambarella, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.7B market cap on $391M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -2.9pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at -28% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 62% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $58M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 25% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 414% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.139324438355851},{"text":"Operating margins softening -2.9pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 28% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (38% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 396% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (AMBA) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/12/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_AMBA_Movement_110926084402_1794275042.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794275042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ambarella (AMBA) Following Edge AI Momentum Questions And A Fair Value Debate","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nasdaq-amba/ambarella/news/ambarella-amba-following-edge-ai-momentum-questions-and-a-fa","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793961064.462,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ambarella (AMBA): A Top 10 Robotics Stock on Sale Down 34%","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ambarella-amba-top-10-robotics-155141674.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793721101.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (AMBA)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_AMBA_103026093402_1793410442.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793410442.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ambarella Shares Slid Even Though Sales Rose","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us